[19.771092, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[19.77112, "o", "  The mailing list has basic mailman3 functionalities like:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[19.771281, "o", "  - Mailing \"reading-group-join@local.edu\" adds users to the list (after confirmation).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[19.771335, "o", "  - Mailing \"reading-group-leave@local.edu\" removes users from the list (after confirmation).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[19.771614, "o", ">   - Mailing \"reading-group@local.edu\" posts an announcement to all subscribers.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   You must save mailman configuration file in /etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   For ease of testing:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[19.771705, "o", "  - Assume all subscriber/user mail addresses follow `<user>@local.edu`, where `<user>`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[19.771804, "o", "  is the local unix username.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[19.77198, "o", "  - Direct user mails to `/var/mail/<username>`. They will be accessed with `mailbox.mbox(f\"/var/mail/{username}\")`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   - List owners do not need to approve join/post requests, i.e., set SubscriptionPolicy.open.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[19.77206, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   Users still need to confirm join/leave by replying though.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
